Adjust the methods I will be giving you to:

- Use dynamic variables for naming (class names, functions, etc.) as much as possible, storing scoped magic values such as __FUNCTION__ and __METHOD__ 
		as variables at the start of the method to be passed accross the scopes;
- Call $this->measureProfile for controller methods, and $this->measure for middlewares method at the main scope of the method and logExecutionTime for critical steps
- Give more well detailed logs for error cases (with ::debug, in a separate call), facilitating latter debugging
- Consider this example for inference:
		```
			public const SHW_LG_FM = 'showLoginForm';
			public function showLoginForm(string $lang = DatabaseConstants::DEFAULT_LANG): View|JsonResponse
			{
				$action = __FUNCTION__;
				return $this->measureProfile($action, function () use ($lang, $action) {
					$output = new ConsoleOutput();
					$base   = class_basename(static::class);
					$msg    = 'Starting login form';
					app()->runningInConsole()
						? $output->writeln("{$msg}")
						: $output->writeln("## {$base}: {$msg}");
					Log::info("[{$base}::{$action}] starting", ['lang_param' => $lang]);
					try {
						$langMsg = 'Processing language';
						app()->runningInConsole()
							? $output->writeln("{$langMsg}")
							: $output->writeln("## {$base}: {$langMsg}");
						Log::info("[{$base}::{$action}] processing language parameter", ['original_lang' => $lang]);
						$lang = self::_setLocale($lang);
						$localeMsg = 'Locale set';
						app()->runningInConsole()
							? $output->writeln("{$localeMsg}")
							: $output->writeln("## {$base}: {$localeMsg}");
						Log::info("[{$base}::{$action}] locale configuration completed", ['final_lang' => $lang]);
						$settingsMsg = 'Loading settings';
						app()->runningInConsole()
							? $output->writeln("{$settingsMsg}")
							: $output->writeln("## {$base}: {$settingsMsg}");
						Log::info("[{$base}::{$action}] retrieving application settings");
						$settings = Utility::settings();
						$viewMsg = 'Rendering view';
						app()->runningInConsole()
							? $output->writeln("{$viewMsg}")
							: $output->writeln("## {$base}: {$viewMsg}");
						$viewPath = self::SINGULAR . '.login';
						Log::info("[{$base}::{$action}] rendering login view", [
							'view_path'    => $viewPath,
							'compact_vars' => [DatabaseConstants::DEFAULT_LANG, DatabaseConstants::TABLE_SETTINGS]
						]);
						$successMsg = "Login form ready for {$viewPath}";
						app()->runningInConsole()
							? $output->writeln("{$successMsg}")
							: $output->writeln("## {$base}: {$successMsg}");
						if (!ViewFacade::exists($viewPath)) {
							$route = Route::getCurrentRoute()?->getName() ?? 'UNDEFINED ROUTE';
							$err   = "Tried to render non-existent view [{$viewPath}] for {$route}";
							Log::error("[{$base}::{$action}] {$err}", [DatabaseConstants::DEFAULT_LANG => $lang]);
							$output->writeln($err);
							return response()->json([
								'error'   => "View [{$viewPath}] does not exist",
								'message' => 'Not found',
								'code'    => '404'
							], 404);
						}
						Log::info("[{$base}::{$action}] login form view created successfully");
						return view($viewPath, [
							DatabaseConstants::DEFAULT_LANG   => $lang,
							DatabaseConstants::TABLE_SETTINGS => $settings,
						]);
					} catch (\Exception $e) {
						$errorMsg = 'Login form failed';
						app()->runningInConsole()
							? $output->writeln("{$errorMsg}: {$e->getMessage()}")
							: $output->writeln("## {$base} ERROR: {$errorMsg}");
						Log::error("[{$base}::{$action}] error in showLoginForm", [
							'error'      => $e->getMessage(),
							'file'       => $e->getFile(),
							'line'       => $e->getLine(),
							'lang_param' => $lang
						]);
						return response()->json([
							'error'   => "View [{$viewPath}] failed to load",
							'message' => 'Server unexpected error: ' . $e->getMessage(),
							'code'    => '500'
						], 500);
					}
				}, ['lang' => $lang]);
			}
		```


	- Don't change ANYTHING in the procedures besides what was asked;
	- Use only single newline between statements/lines, never double or more;
	- Omit brackets when possible;
	- Do any comments, EXCEPT to highlight critical points of failures, and precced then with // !
	- Do not call "use" in any capacity, just comment the imports as suggestions;
	- Omit brackets for one line blocks;
	- NEVER use dynamic/magic variables (e.g.: __FUNCTION__) inside of the closure declaration. If these are used (as it should be in most cases), store these as variables right at the beginning of the method body;
	- In case of controllers, always add a check to see if the View::exists; if it doesn't, just move the user back to where he was, and include a with() describing the 404 as ("HTTP 404: Page ${/* View Name Alias or URL */} not found!");
	- The import comments should always be added before the function signature, not inside the body
